<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<package xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/packaging/2015/06/nuspec.xsd">
  <metadata>
    <id>whoops</id>
    <version>1.0.1</version>
    <title>Whoops</title>
    <authors>Holy Spirit Studios</authors>
    <projectUrl>https://github.com/HolySpiritStudios/whoops</projectUrl>
    <licenseUrl>https://github.com/HolySpiritStudios/whoops/blob/main/LICENSE</licenseUrl>
    <requireLicenseAcceptance>false</requireLicenseAcceptance>
    <tags>powershell terminal safety git history guard psreadline</tags>
    <summary>Guards against accidental re-execution of dangerous terminal commands from history.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Ever scrolled through your terminal history and accidentally hit Enter on `git reset --hard`? Whoops prevents that.

Whoops intercepts dangerous commands recalled from history via PSReadLine. When you arrow-up onto a blocked command and press Enter, it's rejected. Manually typed commands always pass through.

Features:
- Blocks history recall of dangerous commands (Up/Down, Ctrl+R, F8)
- Manually typed commands are never blocked
- Configurable JSON blocklist at ~/.whoops/whoops-blocklist.json
- Ships with git reset --hard blocked by default
- ~15ms overhead per interactive session, zero for automation
]]></description>
  </metadata>
  <files>
    <file src="tools\**" target="tools" />
    <file src="LICENSE" target="tools\LICENSE.txt" />
  </files>
</package>
